    "name": "count-min-a-person-who-joined-part-way-through-the-window",
    "why": "Owner decision L one axis along: a floor evaluates only a WHOLE window, and a window can be partial because of the person as well as because of the data. p-noor joined on the 5th, so the week beginning on the 2nd is not a week they had; judging their single duty against a floor of two would report a shortfall they could not have made up, on their very first block. The window is left unjudged and the row NAMES them, because a skip nobody can see is the same as a rule that did nothing. Their second week starts after they joined and is measured normally, and p-ali's empty second week is what proves the floor still fires on somebody who did have the whole of it. Leave deliberately does NOT work this way — that would be the scaling decision L refuses.",
